course: dictionary
lesson: 16100
title: Words that show how something feels
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you how a thing makes you feel, not just what it looks like. «The walk home seemed endless, and every step felt heavy.» The clues are endless and heavy: the walk is long and it drains your energy. So wearisome means something that makes you feel tired and fed up.
explain: Wearisome is a rather formal word, the kind you meet in books and stories. In everyday talk people often say tiring, boring or tedious. «The wearisome journey took all day in the car.» Try swapping in tiring: «The tiring journey took all day in the car.» It still makes sense, so tiring is a good everyday match.
explain: Look at the ending -some. Wearisome is close to weary, which means tired. A wearisome task wears you out, and a wearisome talk goes on so long that you start to yawn and lose interest.
fact: Wearisome means making you feel tired, bored or fed up, especially because it goes on too long.
fact: «A wearisome journey» is a long trip that seems to drag on.
fact: «A wearisome task» is a dull job that takes a very long time.
fact: Everyday words that mean about the same are tiring, boring and tedious.
fact: Context clues often include words like long, endless or dragged on.
exercise: «The wearisome journey took all day.» What does wearisome mean here? | Cold and wet | Very quick and exciting | Full of bright colours | *Making you feel tired and bored because it goes on too long
exercise: «Sam spent the afternoon on a wearisome task: sorting ten thousand buttons.» Which everyday word could replace wearisome? | Sudden | Loud | Joyful | *Tedious
exercise: Find the word in this sentence that means tired: «The long, wearisome hike left us exhausted.» | hike | long | *exhausted | wearisome
test: «After hours of waiting in the queue, the wearisome wait made Mia yawn and sigh.» What does wearisome suggest? | Quick and easy | Exciting and fun | Bright and cheerful | *Tired and fed up
test: Which of these is a wearisome task? | A quick game of tag at break | *Copying one hundred spellings out by hand | A short story about a dragon | A surprise party with cake
exam: «The speech was so long and wearisome that half the audience fell asleep.» What does wearisome mean? | Clear and very short | Short and funny | Loud and angry | *Long and tiring, making people bored
